  Nominal amplitude, life (stage_e.py):   sa = (1-R)/2 * peak / KT_B = 0.45 * peak / 1.66  (R = 0.1, KT_B = 1.66)
  Nominal amplitude, limit state (fatigue.py g_fun): sn = peak/KT_B; sa = (1-R)/2*sn = 0.45*peak/1.66 -> identical
  Resistance, life:        sa_fail(1e6) = A*scale*1e6^b = (A*1e6^b/450) * ratio*UTS   [no Kf, no per-sample mean stress]
  Resistance, limit state: allow = ratio*UTS/Kf * (1 - sm/UTS) (Goodman) or *(1-(sm/UTS)^2) (Gerber), sm = (1+R)/2*sn = 0.55*peak/1.66, Kf = Kt = 1.66
  Differences: (i) Kf: 1.66 in the limit state, not explicit in the life line; (ii) the mean-stress correction is recomputed per sample (via sm and UTS_i) in the limit state, and fixed at the Table 2 endpoint in V1.

